From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: Let a submit run for seconds before hangcheck kills it

msm declares a GPU hang when a submit's fence has not advanced for two
hangcheck periods without command-stream progress, and caps any submit
at four periods even while the CP advances. On a6xx and later the
period is half of DRM_MSM_HANGCHECK_DEFAULT_PERIOD, 250 ms: no submit
may run longer than about 1 s, and one long dispatch is killed after
about 0.5 s.

Signed-off-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
---
retroforge: not posted.
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.h
@@ -241,7 +241,8 @@
 	 */
 #define DRM_MSM_INACTIVE_PERIOD   66 /* in ms (roughly four frames) */
 
-#define DRM_MSM_HANGCHECK_DEFAULT_PERIOD 500 /* in ms */
+/* Long enough for a multi-second submit on a slow GPU (A610) */
+#define DRM_MSM_HANGCHECK_DEFAULT_PERIOD 6000 /* in ms */
 #define DRM_MSM_HANGCHECK_PROGRESS_RETRIES 3
 	struct timer_list hangcheck_timer;
 
